      "content": "it doesnt feel like a mistake someone can just \"process\" in therapy. it feels like a permanent fact. like, the damage is done and i'm still here just existing, which feels wrong. how can anyone keep going after they realize they're fundamentally broken? it feels like the world would just be cleaner if i wasn't in it anymore.",
